         "Rage of Mechs is a multiplayer turn-based strategy game set in a post-apocalyptic world. Customize your Mechs and fight in tactical arena battles against other players. Every move matters. Outsmart, outmaneuver, and dominate the arena.",
         "Welcome to Rage of Mechs Rage of Mechs is a turn-based strategy game inspired by classics like XCOM, Jagged Alliance, Fallout, Heroes of Might and Magic III, and BattleTech. Early Access The game is currently in early alpha. A lot of core systems are already in place, but we’re just getting started. We have big plans ahead and a clear development roadmap to guide them. Team Assembly There are no hard limits on the number of units in your squad—only weight. Each weapon and module adds to the total weight of your Mech, and the combined weight of all your Mechs determines your team’s limit. Balancing firepower, utility, and mobility is up to you. Build Your Mech Every Mech is fully modular and uniquely customizable. Inspired by the way firearms are assembled in real life — with attachments like grips, silencers, and optics — we’ve built a system that lets you swap out weapons, engines, armor, cooling systems, camouflage units, radar arrays, and more. Each choice affects performance on the battlefield. Pilots Each Mech is piloted by a Paladin — a warrior bonded to their machine. While pilot abilities, factions, and mood systems are still under development, our goal is to introduce specialized skills, interpersonal relationships, and faction-based buffs and debuffs. Paladins will be more than stats — they’ll be characters. Multiplayer, Turn-Based Combat We’re passionate about turn-based gameplay and wanted to bring it into a competitive, multiplayer setting. Rage of Mechs blends tactical depth with head-to-head battles, where every decision counts. Environments and Tactical Terrain We’ve implemented dynamic maps with day/night cycles and varying terrain types. At night, visibility is reduced — just like in real life — making ambushes and stealth tactics more viable. Forests slow your movement but improve camouflage. Water cools your Mech but can be dangerous to cross. Terrain isn’t just decoration; it’s part of your strategy. Join the Community We’re building Rage of Mechs alongside our players. Your feedback, ideas, and insights are vital to us. Join our official Discord and help shape the game. We want to create something great—with you, not just for you! Join today and become a Paladin :) ",
         "Welcome to Rage of Mechs Rage of Mechs is a turn-based strategy game inspired by classics like XCOM, Jagged Alliance, Fallout, Heroes of Might and Magic III, and BattleTech. Early Access The game is currently in early alpha. A lot of core systems are already in place, but we’re just getting started. We have big plans ahead and a clear development roadmap to guide them. Team Assembly There are no hard limits on the number of units in your squad—only weight. Each weapon and module adds to the total weight of your Mech, and the combined weight of all your Mechs determines your team’s limit. Balancing firepower, utility, and mobility is up to you. Build Your Mech Every Mech is fully modular and uniquely customizable. Inspired by the way firearms are assembled in real life — with attachments like grips, silencers, and optics — we’ve built a system that lets you swap out weapons, engines, armor, cooling systems, camouflage units, radar arrays, and more. Each choice affects performance on the battlefield. Pilots Each Mech is piloted by a Paladin — a warrior bonded to their machine. While pilot abilities, factions, and mood systems are still under development, our goal is to introduce specialized skills, interpersonal relationships, and faction-based buffs and debuffs. Paladins will be more than stats — they’ll be characters. Multiplayer, Turn-Based Combat We’re passionate about turn-based gameplay and wanted to bring it into a competitive, multiplayer setting. Rage of Mechs blends tactical depth with head-to-head battles, where every decision counts. Environments and Tactical Terrain We’ve implemented dynamic maps with day/night cycles and varying terrain types. At night, visibility is reduced — just like in real life — making ambushes and stealth tactics more viable. Forests slow your movement but improve camouflage. Water cools your Mech but can be dangerous to cross. Terrain isn’t just decoration; it’s part of your strategy. Join the Community We’re building Rage of Mechs alongside our players. Your feedback, ideas, and insights are vital to us. Join our official Discord and help shape the game. We want to create something great—with you, not just for you! Join today and become a Paladin :) ",
